  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2023 Safe Mobility Office (SMO) initiative in Guatemala, Colombia, Costa Rica, and Ecuador</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through the Safe Mobility Offices established in locations across the targeted countries in Central and South America, individuals are provided with information on access to accelerated resettlement processing and to information on other lawful pathways. This initiative gives individuals alternatives to making hazardous journeys to the Mexico- United States border by providing safer lawful options to migrate and will protect them from smuggling, exploitation and other forms of violence or abuses throughout their migration journey. Through this project, IOM will provide essential assistance to those eligible for resettlement pathway in Colombia, Costa Rica, Ecuador and Guatemala, providing the conditions for migrants and refugees to meet basic needs while they wait for their resettlement case to be processed. This project facilitates the access to cash and voucher assistance, healthcare assistance and shelter and accommodation support by those who are eligible for resettlement to the United States or other countries that offer such opportunities.</narrative>
  </description>
